<resources>
    <!--
      Night override of the window dressing only — the UI itself is styled by
      PowerViewTheme in Compose, not from here.

      The point is the frame between the window opening and Compose drawing
      anything. AppCompat's night background is a mid grey, so on the OLED
      theme every cold start flashes grey before turning black. Black here
      removes that.

      Two honest limitations. This applies to *both* dark themes, since a
      resource qualifier can only see the system's night setting and not the
      app's own ThemeMode — harmless, because the standard dark scheme's
      surfaces are nearly this dark anyway. And someone running the OLED theme
      with the system in light mode still gets a light first frame, for the
      same reason. Fixing either properly means recreating the activity on a
      theme change, which is a lot of machinery for one frame.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.PowerView" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/black</item>
    </style>
</resources>
